se,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.36153,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Tempus AI, Inc. operates as a healthcare technology company in the United States. It offers the Tempus platform, a closed-loop, full-stack, bi-directional integrations between a clinician's desktop and its laboratory diagnostic capabilities, analytics platform, and repository of multimodal data; and Hub, a clinical application for physicians and other healthcare providers for use in the diagnostics product line as an end-to-end application for healthcare providers for NGS tests. The company also provides Lens, a software application for life sciences and advanced precision research; diagnostics services, such as NGS diagnostics, PCR profiling, and other anatomic and molecular pathology tests; and large-panel solid tumor and hematologic testing through multiple assays, with its core clinical assay (xT and xR) offering large panel DNA, RNA full transcriptome, and incidental germline findings through normal blood or saliva analyses. In addition, it provides genetic tests focused on inherited conditions; an nP assay for pharmacogenomic testing for patients with psychiatric conditions, including depression, general anxiety disorder, bipolar disorder, and other relevant diagnoses; Insights, which licenses libraries of linked, de-identified clinical, molecular, and imaging data; Organoids, a tumor derived biological modeling. Further, the company offers Trials for clinical trial matching services; Next, an AI platform; Algos, an algorithm-based diagnostics application. It has Strategic Collaborations with AstraZeneca AB, Pathos AI, Inc., GlaxoSmithKline, Merck, and Recursion Pharmaceuticals, Inc. Additionally, it also has a strategic collaboration with Blood Cancer United to develop registry for pediatric acute myeloid leukemia. The company was formerly known as Tempus Labs, Inc. and changed its name to Tempus AI, Inc. in January 2023. Tempus AI, Inc. was incorporated in 2015 and is headquartered in Chicago, Illinois.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Eric P. Lefkofsky J.D. | Co-Founder, CEO, President & Chairman | Age 55 | Compensation: $1.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $335K ranks in the below the sector median among Healthcare peers. Stock-based compensation of $33K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Tempus AI, Inc. is a large-cap healthcare business with a $13.1B market cap on $1.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +83% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","The company is burning through $239M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -3.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 36% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (24.1% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Operating margins 19% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $74.2M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 572% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Growing faster than most Healthcare peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Tempest Minerals (ASX:TEM) Field Programmes Hunt for Follow-Up Targets","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/stocks/penny/tempest-minerals-asxtem-field-programmes-hunt-for-follow-up-targets","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794558600.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.25,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Tempest Minerals (ASX:TEM): Can Field Programmes Find Targets Worth Chasing?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/stocks/penny/tempest-minerals-asxtem-can-field-programmes-find-targets-worth-chasing","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794466320.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.026,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What Tempus AI (TEM)'s Military Cancer Car